@@ -694,6 +694,31 @@ graph.addCopyPass({
 });
 ```
 
+### Clearing and reading buffers with ready-made copy nodes
+
+Transient buffers are not zero-initialized, and logical transients with disjoint lifetimes share
+physical bytes, so an operation that accumulates into a transient (atomics, partial writes) needs
+an explicit clear first. `createGPUClearBufferCommandNode()` builds that copy node, and
+`createGPUReadbackCommandNode()` builds a node that copies a transient or imported range into a
+`GPUReadbackTicket` at the point of the schedule where it holds its value:
+
+```ts
+graph.add(createGPUClearBufferCommandNode({id: 'zero-bins', target: binsHandle}));
+// ... nodes that accumulate into binsHandle ...
+graph.add(
+  createGPUReadbackCommandNode({
+    id: 'read-bins',
+    source: binsHandle,
+    getTicket: parameters => parameters.ticket
+  })
+);
+```
+
+`compiled.preflight.uninitializedTransientReads` lists every transient buffer whose first
+scheduled access is a read, so a missing clear shows up before submission. Writes are tracked per
+buffer, not per byte range, so a partially written transient is reported only when nothing wrote it
+at all.
+
 ### Explicit dependencies and repeated encodings
 
 Prefer declared resource uses because they explain both ordering and transient lifetimes. Add
